	(text "BLUE pin - Signal	[connector pin 1]\nRED pin - 5V		[connector pin 2]\nBLACK pin - GND		[connector pin 3]\n\nNote: The module usually has a tiny switch on it labeled \"A / D\".\n\"A\" (Analog): Gives you a voltage curve based on how dirty the water is.\n\"D\" (Digital): Just gives a High/Low signal if the water is \"too dirty\"\nFor your circuit: Ensure the physical switch is set to \"A\"."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 63.754 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
